  "summary": "I am a people focused problem solver and leader with a passion for simple solutions. I've spent my career working in difficult technical situations and have developed a keen eye for how software evolves (or degrades) over years of development. I've proposed and implemented large scale architectural refactors that greatly simplified the product, improved performance, and enabled development teams to work with a much more consistent velocity. I believe that communication, clarity, and shared goals are the fundamentals that create success for a software team over the long term.\n\nI've also developed a reputation as a Swiss Army knife that can reach far outside of Software roles. I've led efforts to develop modern EHR integrations with FHIR, culminating in a demonstration at the #HIMSS 2019 Interoperability Showcase along with 5 other organizations. I've guided external data vendors through an onboarding process and given them quarterly updates on the status of their data. Finally, I've led a 10 person team that built pipelines for enterprise, HIPAA compliant data sets (pharmacy claims, medical claims, EHR, etc.) from the largest healthcare companies in the country.",
